::ingredients

(pork shoulder, boneless) 2 1/2lb
(garlic, slivers) 6 cloves
(cumin) 1 1/2tsp
(sazon) 1/2tsp
(oregano, dry) 1/4tsp
(chicken broth, low sodium) 3/4 cup
(chipotle peppers, in adobo sauce) 2-3
(bay leaf) 2
(adobo seasoning, dry) 1/4tsp
# Method-only seasonings
(salt, kosher) as needed
(pepper) as needed

::equipment

(sauté pan, medium)
(knife, sharp)
(slow cooker)
(fork) 2

::instructions

(pork shoulder) + (salt) + (pepper) <season>
    <brown, medium sauté pan, medium-high heat, all sides>
    <remove from heat>
    <cool, ~10m>
    <pierce, sharp knife, small holes>
    + (garlic) <insert, slivers as far into holes as possible>
(chicken broth) <pour, slow cooker>
{carnitas} = (chicken broth) + (pork shoulder) + (garlic)
{carnitas} + (cumin) + (adobo seasoning) + (sazon) + (oregano) <season>
    + (bay leaf) + (chipotle peppers)
    <cover>
    <slow cook, low, 8h>
(pork shoulder) <shred, 2 forks>
{carnitas} <mix, pork with juices>
    <cook, another 15-30m>

::story
This recipe makes a lot and is super easy. A whole roast usually makes enough for a few meals (depending on how many people will be eating it).

::notes
Leftovers can be refrigerated for 4-5 days.

